#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054363 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "228b0a63-bf0e-57bf-aa1e-ef5518236462" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Mathematical Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "db1f7851-43e9-5fee-9553-f9d6ead38b40" :question/math-academy-id "e-12675" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P$: Compute the product of the first four prime numbers.\n\n- $Q$: Four is a prime number.\n\n- $R$: Is four a prime number?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false. Rather, it is an instruction.\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $4$ is not a prime number (it is divisible by $2$).\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false. Rather, it is a question, and the possible answers are \"yes\" or \"no.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054364 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f185774-4d55-515c-9032-8f6832c6999a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Truth Value of a Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "8ca6e60c-1411-5f6e-a9f4-d6209f847ddf" :question/math-academy-id "e-12676" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P:$ $4$ is a positive number.\n\n- $Q:$ $2^3$ is a natural number.\n\n- $R:$ $-4 \\geq 2$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *true.* Indeed, $4$ is a positive number.\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *true.* Indeed,  $2^3=8$ is a natural number.\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $-4 \\ngeq 2$ .\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054367 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/id #uuid "d85fd26e-50f6-58f1-9e44-8df23863ee6a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12685" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P: \\{5,6,7\\}\\cap \\{6,8,10\\} = \\{6\\}$\n\n- $Q: \\sqrt{3} +2$\n\n- $R: 4\\mid 2$\n\n**Note**: The notation \n\n$$\na\\mid b\n$$\n\nmeans \"$a$ divides $b.$\" This is equivalent to the statement that $b$ is divisible by $a.$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because the intersection of the given sets is indeed the set $\\{6\\}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $4$ does not divide $2$ (i.e., $2$ is not divisible by $4$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates"}] :question/id #uuid "a70765b4-08b9-5ebf-92f4-1b7c5266523e" :question/math-academy-id "e-13288" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\nI. Subtract $x$ from $10.$\n\nII. $y^2 -2  \\leq 3$\n\nIII. $1+z$ is a perfect square." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it gives an instruction.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "228b0a63-bf0e-57bf-aa1e-ef5518236462" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Mathematical Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d281e4c-12f3-5079-93f5-be66bce4c00b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Compute the sum of the first two natural numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399366} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc90903-d3c5-5540-9c56-a82ad70a2ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set of rational numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399367} {:answer/id #uuid "e4002685-8407-5008-9596-c51979ab7920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The diagonal of a quadrilateral." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399368} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdda3a7-d2ed-58bf-a55c-bd1037a65ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ is a rational number." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399369} {:answer/id #uuid "4a90792e-413a-5402-b9c4-94db6437b94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "What is a prime number?" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbdda3a7-d2ed-58bf-a55c-bd1037a65ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ is a rational number." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399369} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c7d492-3fd1-55b7-9667-7d1d03627d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b625ee5e-9a08-5485-b20f-479dacadfb89" :question/math-academy-id "q-102843" :question/problem "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"$1$ is a rational number.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "228b0a63-bf0e-57bf-aa1e-ef5518236462" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Mathematical Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27e7f1a2-0340-57ea-a3ec-6b7f16d5e4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A rectangle has four angles." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559114} {:answer/id #uuid "2a6a5fdc-fdac-5d72-9181-7f0590bf65a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sides of a triangle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559124} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7642cc-29be-5f1a-9a16-ef318c444413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Sum of the measures of the angles in a pentagon." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559281} {:answer/id #uuid "b67f3de7-0824-5db8-a89a-109dbb1c1bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The diameter of a circle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559472} {:answer/id #uuid "ee24fb1c-29c7-5fc5-9eae-4512b626a3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "How do you find the perimeter of a square?" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27e7f1a2-0340-57ea-a3ec-6b7f16d5e4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A rectangle has four angles." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559114} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9bbce88-e20f-53a3-b5e8-17d8d8b20865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae9ba4f6-2cb2-5711-bd11-5c1b1d70436a" :question/math-academy-id "q-102847" :question/problem "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"A rectangle has four angles.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f185774-4d55-515c-9032-8f6832c6999a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Truth Value of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28af8068-389d-58ea-af5e-aa10b40c5b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559119} {:answer/id #uuid "5b8b0d6b-7ed6-501b-94e1-080108062fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Possible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559253} {:answer/id #uuid "96c1fe5f-0cb0-58bb-adc0-7dcf2f36b957" :answer/type {:db