r-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a13c06f-6317-5f54-a60c-2244cd05e4c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-170843" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n- **P.** $P:2\\,|\\,4$\n- **Q.** $Q:\\sqrt{2}\\in N$\n- **R.** $R:2+2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $2$ divides $4.$\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $\\sqrt{2}$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "552218e3-b220-58c3-8c75-5b10d4776417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459611} {:answer/id #uuid "4d32738d-a847-5c0a-850c-c2e3237e0d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d32738d-a847-5c0a-850c-c2e3237e0d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459612} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d2462b7-7be9-5abc-a127-8af98e06b645" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "