hematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because the intersection of the given sets is empty.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *false* since $4$ is not prime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ca2b5c-6791-591f-abda-f27884967edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459617} {:answer/id #uuid "c56bf6b0-66f4-518a-a6ce-ba874d1a9c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56bf6b0-66f4-518a-a6ce-ba874d1a9c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459618} :answer-field/id #uuid "24a6ed8a-17b7-51a7-bb49-dcf74e7ade9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04cb5f8b-73b3-5617-abfc-6b43148614ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459619} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8f35e0-edab-543a-a110-589cb05bd8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f8f35e0-edab-543a-a110-589cb05bd8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459620} :answer-field/id #uuid "96184caa-a44f-51b9-bafe-5eddcc9cb49b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acb09f9b-41e0-580c-a041-095bbce4770b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459621} {:answer/id #uuid "868a0a7e-8c6e-5345-b4ea-51218d4e274a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acb09f9b-41e0-580c-a041-095bbce4770b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459621} :answer-field/id #uuid "42968c23-3a57-5e5b-b613-c57e6362a57d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5327827-bdd3-59f2-8ac3-6f2fcb1af21e" :question/math-academy-id "q-171486" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n- **I.** $P(n):$ $n$ is even.\n- **II.** $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}-x\\ge 1$\n- **III.** $R(y):$ Draw a line of width $y\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give an instruction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f185774-4d55-515c-9032-8f6832c6999a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Truth Value of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2303e8fc-c1dc-524c-9411-1f4a00def4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559101} {:answer/id #uuid "3b022a5e-ac82-54c3-b12b-4abc34d6c281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559163} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc17bbe-8dd6-5f5a-9886-4d726f015772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P,Q,$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559287} {:answer/id #uuid "9517b839-199e-5857-8086-d5bd10fd12f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559387} {:answer/id #uuid "f74b8f84-001c-5bd3-858c-127b607a4caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b022a5e-ac82-54c3-b12b-4abc34d6c281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559163} :answer-field/id #uuid "f65721db-6112-5108-9ea1-45e3d318fab2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4bf832a-fa7c-5bf9-96bc-b8972c38ecca" :question/math-academy-id "q-173721" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are false?\n\n- $P:$ $\\sqrt{5}$ is a real number.\n\n- $Q:$ $10$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- $R:$ $2+3\\le 1$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *true.* Indeed, $\\sqrt{5}$ is a real number.\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *false* because $10$ is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $2+3=5≰1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f185774-4d55-515c-9032-8f6832c6999a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Truth Value of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36967bc3-fba1-5c19-87b7-c7a780a3ef5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559155} {:answer/id #uuid "473c2134-347a-5352-8a92-c8abb336f0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559200} {:answer/id #uuid "57fc1f02-0cb6-58ff-a2f3-430b7606eb5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559244} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ae0e82-5fd8-5122-b6e2-9044559ff78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559424} {:answer/id #uuid "d58f599c-20dc-5023-ba78-635c62a7f31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045